Yi∼Poisson(λi×Ni)log⁡(λi)=a+β_srsf2+β_dnmt3a+β_AZD+β_srsf2×dnmt3a+β_srsf2×AZD+β_dnmt3a×AZD+u_rep
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{gathered}Y_{i} \sim \operatorname{Poisson}\left(\lambda_{i} \times N_{i}\right) \\ \log \left(\lambda_{i}\right)=a+\beta \_ \text {srsf } 2+\beta \_d n m t 3 a+\beta \_A Z D+\beta \_ \text {srsf } 2 \times d n m t 3 a+\beta \_ \text {srsf } 2 \times A Z D+\beta \_d n m t 3 a \times A Z D+ \\ \text { u_rep }\end{gathered}$$\end{document}

To assess the effects of CRISPR editing, AZD7648 treatment, and donor sex on the probability of a cell carrying at least one structural variant event, we fitted three independent Bayesian mixed-effects binary outcome models: one for del/dup events prior to stringent filtering (5 Mb size threshold), one for del/dup events after final filtering (≥10% chromosome arm, arm-weakness filter applied), and one for inversion events (arm-weakness filter with shared-control blacklist at reciprocal overlap ≥0.6). All models were implemented in brms (v2.23.0) on R (v4.4.3) with Stan as the MCMC backend. The response variable was a binary indicator of whether each cell carried at least one retained event of the relevant SV class (0 = event-negative, 1 = event-positive). The linear predictor on the log-odds scale was:


logit(πi)=a+β−SRSF2×SRSF2i+β−DNMT3A×DNMT3Ai+β−mol×AZD7648i+β−SRSF2:mol×(SRSF2i×AZD7648i)+β−DNMT3A:mol×(DNMT3Ai×AZD7648i)+β−SRSF2:DNMT3A×(SRSF2i×DNMT3Ai)+β−SRSF2:DNMT3A:mol×(SRSF2i×DNMT3Ai×AZD7648+β−sex× sex i+u_replicate[repi]
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{gathered}\operatorname{logit}\left(\pi_{i}\right)=a+\beta_{-} S R S F 2 \times S R S F 2_{i}+\beta_{-} D N M T 3 A \times D N M T 3 A_{i} \\ +\beta_{-} m o l \times A Z D 7648_{i} \\ +\beta_{-} S R S F 2: m o l \times\left(S R S F 2_{i} \times A Z D 7648_{i}\right) \\ +\beta_{-} D N M T 3 A: m o l \times\left(D N M T 3 A_{i} \times A Z D 7648_{i}\right) \\ +\beta_{-} S R S F 2: D N M T 3 A \times\left(S R S F 2_{i} \times D N M T 3 A_{i}\right) \\ +\beta_{-} S R S F 2: D N M T 3 A: \operatorname{mol} \times\left(S R S F 2_{i} \times D N M T 3 A_{i} \times A Z D 7648\right. \\ +\beta_{-} s e x \times \text { sex }_{i} \\ +u \_ \text {replicate }\left[r e p_{i}\right]\end{gathered}$$\end{document}
